    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "There are different types of ammunition available for the weapons. The two most common types are FMJ (full metal jacket) and JHP (jacketed hollow point). In general, bullets of FMJ type remain more intact when they hit and penetrate objects. JHP bullets deform more on impact and cause more damage to soft targets.\n\nThe deformation (or lack thereof) of a bullet translates into how easily it penetrates the materials it hits."
