  m_Text: JHP bullets do considerably more damage to unarmored targets than FMJ rounds do. This is because they expand to a larger diameter and therefore disrupt a lot more tissue when they penetrate. Often they are able to transfer a lot more of their energy to the targets they hit. As a result they don't penetrate nearly as far as FMJ rounds do.
