    m_Alignment: 3
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "Use precision mode to control bullets you fire. When precision mode is active the bullets will only be able to cause damage within a specific distance from the weapon. This distance is denoted by two extra dots that appear around the cursor.\n\nPrecision mode allows you to fire past targets that you don't want to hit. It is also useful to avoid causing harm to unintended targets beyond the one you are firing at. Bullets that are not in precision mode will harm everything along their entire paths. Most bullets easily penetrate doors, walls and tissue and continue on the other side, so injuring unintended targets is a risk when not using precision mode."
